 "confidence": "inferred",
 "uncertainty_m": 12,
 "uncertainty_note": "The fit's RMS is 4.2 m and its worst control point 9.4 m; the ridge follower's own scatter about a 3-4 px ink line adds about 2 m. 12 m is those in quadrature rounded up, and it is smaller than the +/- 20 m data/sources/thompson_plat_1830.json declares for the dataset as a whole because that figure covers building from the sheet and this covers only reading a line off it.",
 "what_was_read": "Thompson draws each bank as ONE freehand ink line on bare paper \u2014 no wash, no fill, nothing to threshold between \u2014 so the reading follows the line rather than the region. The banks are the only freehand curves on an otherwise entirely ruled sheet, which is what makes a ridge follower safe here and would make it unsafe on Wright.",
